# apps/reading/.env.example
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and customise.
# Loaded by Vite at build time.

# UI cutover flag (S12).
#
# Default: v2 — the redesigned four-workflow shell: NavRail
# (Research · Read · Write · Speak) + the Topbar chrome + the
# workflow-scoped content tree + the products launcher
# (src/AppShell.tsx, mounted by src/main.tsx → src/App.tsx).
#
# Rollback: set VITE_ANTIEK_UI=v1 in the production env and redeploy.
# v1 renders src/AppLegacy.tsx — the intentionally-minimal pre-redesign
# chrome, a tiny target if the new shell breaks in prod. The flag is the
# reversible-change discipline: one env var + a Cloudflare Pages
# redeploy, no code change. Retiring v1 + the flag is a later operator
# decision once the new IA is proven in prod.
VITE_ANTIEK_UI=v2

# PostHog product analytics (EU). Copy token from PostHog project settings.
# Omit both vars to disable analytics (default in CI / Storybook).
# VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=phc_...
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# Optional: override the substrate base URL when running the dev
# server against a non-localhost backend.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000

# Optional: enable Storybook addon-a11y on Storybook bootup.
# (No-op for dev / build server.)
# VITE_STORYBOOK_A11Y=1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mountain Shell SPR-02 — Krea scene-art proxy.
#
# These are BACKEND (server-side) env vars, documented here for the
# operator + the ansible inventory. They are NOT Vite vars and MUST NEVER
# be prefixed VITE_ (a VITE_ prefix would bake the secret into the browser
# bundle — the exact failure this proxy exists to prevent). The browser
# only ever talks to /krea/* (proxied in dev by vite.config.ts); it never
# sees the token. With NO token set, the whole substrate runs in the
# deterministic offline-fallback path (the default in dev / CI / sandbox).
#
#   KREA_API_TOKEN        Krea bearer token (server-side ONLY). Absent →
#                         /krea/* returns a typed 503 "disabled" signal and
#                         the background renders the deterministic
#                         placeholder. DO NOT COMMIT A REAL KEY.
#   KREA_KILL_SWITCH      Operator panic lever. 1/true/yes/on → every
#                         generation falls back regardless of key.
#   ANTIEK_KREA_BASE_URL  Override the Krea base URL (default
#                         https://api.krea.ai) for proxying / a host change.
#   KREA_DAILY_UNIT_CAP   Max image generations/day (default 50; one image
#                         ≈ one compute unit ≈ ~$0.04, so 50/day ≈ ~$2/day,
#                         ~half the ~100-unit free tier). 0 = block all.
#   KREA_RATE_LIMIT_MAX   Max submissions per 60s window (default 6; Flux is
#                         ~4s/image so ~6/min is generous for one operator
#                         yet caps a runaway loop).
#   KREA_CACHE_TTL_S      Scene-art cache TTL in seconds (default 3600). An
#                         identical scene-state within the TTL is served from
#                         cache and never re-billed.
#
# KREA_API_TOKEN=         # set ONLY in the gitignored server env, never here
# KREA_KILL_SWITCH=
# ANTIEK_KREA_BASE_URL=https://api.krea.ai
# KREA_DAILY_UNIT_CAP=50
# KREA_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=6
# KREA_CACHE_TTL_S=3600

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DRW gather mode (SPR-DRL-08) — BACKEND (server-side) env vars.
#
# The Deep Research Workflow's per-sub-question gather loop. Documented
# here for the operator + the ansible inventory; these are NOT Vite vars
# and MUST NEVER be prefixed VITE_ (a VITE_ prefix would bake EXA_API_KEY
# into the browser bundle).
#
#   ANTIEK_DRW_GATHER     Selects the gather loop. Default `stub`.
#                         - stub: the contract gather placeholder — emits
#                           honest StepEvents but does NO real retrieval.
#                           The safe prod default; never needs a key.
#                         - exa: the real Exa Wedge-1 discovery loop.
#                           Runs `discover` then `promote_discovery` for
#                           the top proposals, routing through the single
#                           ingest_url write seam + the legal gate, so the
#                           evidence pack carries real doc-url-* chunks.
#                           Requires EXA_API_KEY.
#   EXA_API_KEY           Exa bearer token (server-side ONLY). Required
#                         when ANTIEK_DRW_GATHER=exa. Absent → the Exa loop
#                         raises on its first `discover` call (no silent
#                         degrade). DO NOT COMMIT A REAL KEY. CI never sets
#                         this — tests inject httpx.MockTransport.
#   EXA_DAILY_BUDGET_USD  Daily Exa spend cap (default 5). Each `discover`
#                         pre-reserves its optimistic cost; exceeding the
#                         cap raises DiscoveryBudgetExceeded with NO silent
#                         fallback (per integration spec §6.7). Raise to
#                         relax.
#
# ANTIEK_DRW_GATHER=stub
# EXA_API_KEY=            # set ONLY in the gitignored server env, never here
# EXA_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5
